From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:45:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: return the error of a radar detection request

The nl80211 driver logs the kernel error of a failed radar detection
request and returns -1 for every failure. A caller then cannot tell a
busy kernel from a failed request. For a background radar request,
the kernel answers -EBUSY while it keeps a chain with a pending CAC,
and a caller that tracks that chain must keep its state.

Return the kernel error instead. A caller that tests the result for
nonzero sees no change.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -11686,7 +11686,7 @@ static int nl80211_start_radar_detection
 
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "nl80211: Failed to start radar detection: "
 		   "%d (%s)", ret, strerror(-ret));
-	return -1;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 
